<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Winter Driving in a Rental: A Pickup Checklist for Western Wisconsin</h1>
<p>Five minutes at the counter and a few things in the back seat make a winter trip on I-94 a lot less stressful.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>The first real snow usually shows up in Jackson County before Thanksgiving, and it doesn't leave until spring. Whether you're renting for a holiday trip, a work week in Eau Claire, or while your own car is in the shop, a little prep at pickup goes a long way on I-94 and the county roads.</p>
<h2>At the counter: a 5-minute walkaround</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Wipers and washer fluid.</strong> Give the wipers a test run and spray the washer before you pull out. Slush off a semi on I-94 will empty a reservoir fast.</li>
<li><strong>Heat and defrost.</strong> Make sure you know where front and rear defrost are. Ask us to point out heated seats or mirrors if the vehicle has them.</li>
<li><strong>Lights.</strong> In December it's dark before 5 PM. Find the headlight and fog light controls before you need them.</li>
<li><strong>Mirrors, seat, phone.</strong> Set everything up in the lot, not on the highway on-ramp.</li>
</ul>
<p>Not sure where something is? Ask. We'd rather spend two minutes walking you through a vehicle than have you hunting for the defrost button at 60 mph.</p>
<h2>Pack a small winter kit</h2>
<p>Bring your own snow brush and scraper so you know you have one. Add a warm blanket, gloves and a hat, a phone charger, water, and a few snacks. A small shovel and a bag of kitty litter for traction take up almost no room in an SUV or minivan, and they are worth it if you end up in a snowy ditch on a back road.</p>
<h2>Check the road before you go</h2>
<p><a href="https://511wi.gov" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;" rel="noopener">511 Wisconsin</a> shows live road conditions, closures, and crashes on I-94, Highway 54, and the state routes around Black River Falls. Check it before you leave and again before the drive home. Bridges and overpasses freeze first, so ease off well before you reach them, and leave a lot more room than you would in July.</p>
<h2>Pick the vehicle for the trip</h2>
<p>For in-town errands and plowed highways, an <a href="/cheap-car-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">intermediate</a> or <a href="/full-size-car-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">full-size car</a> handles winter fine at $55 or $65/day for local renters, with unlimited mileage. For rural driveways, gravel roads, or a trip with snow in the forecast, our <a href="/suv-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">two Ford Edge SUVs and the AWD Subaru Outback</a> run $80/day or $480/week for local renters, with unlimited mileage. Non-local rates are intermediate $75/day or $450/week, full-size $85/day or $510/week, and SUV/AWD $100/day or $600/week, plus a per-mile charge. Call 715-396-1466 for the per-mile rate. Local means residents of Black River Falls and Jackson County, WI. One honest note: all-wheel drive helps you get moving. It doesn't help you stop. Read <a href="/blog/winter-awd-rental-subaru-outback-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">when AWD is worth it</a> before you decide.</p>
<h2>If the weather changes your plans</h2>
<p>Storms move return dates. If a blizzard means you'd rather wait a day, call 715-396-1466 before your scheduled return so we can sort it out together. In an emergency, call 911 first. Our hours are Monday to Friday 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM, Saturday 8:00 AM to noon, and Sunday closed. After-hours drop-off returns are available.</p>
<p><strong>Call or text 715-396-1466</strong> to reserve. Family-owned in Black River Falls since 1983.</p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Do I need an AWD rental for winter driving in Wisconsin?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Not always. A front-wheel-drive car handles plowed highways and in-town driving well. An AWD Subaru Outback or Ford Edge SUV is the better pick for rural driveways, gravel roads, and trips with snow in the forecast. AWD helps you get moving but does not shorten stopping distance.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Should I bring my own snow brush and scraper?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Bring your own so you know you have one, along with a blanket, gloves, a phone charger, water, and snacks.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Where can I check road conditions near Black River Falls?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>511 Wisconsin (511wi.gov) shows live conditions, closures, and crashes on I-94, Highway 54, and nearby state highways.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What if winter weather delays my return?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Call 715-396-1466 before your scheduled return time so we can work out a new plan. In an emergency, call 911 first.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
